-- Nothing raised: no ground, by either composition.
#ASSERT NOT (`a ground for refusal other than section 3 no. 4 applies` `grounds with nothing raised`)
#ASSERT NOT (`a ground for refusal other than a statutory duty applies` `grounds with nothing raised`)
-- Each of the grounds other than § 3 no. 4 is raised alone: both compositions say a ground applies.
#ASSERT `a ground for refusal other than section 3 no. 4 applies` `grounds with only section 3 no. 1 raised`
#ASSERT `a ground for refusal other than a statutory duty applies` `grounds with only section 3 no. 1 raised`
#ASSERT `a ground for refusal other than section 3 no. 4 applies` `grounds with only section 3 no. 2 raised`
#ASSERT `a ground for refusal other than a statutory duty applies` `grounds with only section 3 no. 2 raised`
#ASSERT `a ground for refusal other than section 3 no. 4 applies` `grounds with only section 3 no. 3 raised`
#ASSERT `a ground for refusal other than a statutory duty applies` `grounds with only section 3 no. 3 raised`
#ASSERT `a ground for refusal other than section 3 no. 4 applies` `grounds with only section 3 no. 5 raised`
#ASSERT `a ground for refusal other than a statutory duty applies` `grounds with only section 3 no. 5 raised`
#ASSERT `a ground for refusal other than section 3 no. 4 applies` `grounds with only section 3 no. 6 raised`
#ASSERT `a ground for refusal other than a statutory duty applies` `grounds with only section 3 no. 6 raised`
#ASSERT `a ground for refusal other than section 3 no. 4 applies` `grounds with only section 3 no. 7 raised`
#ASSERT `a ground for refusal other than a statutory duty applies` `grounds with only section 3 no. 7 raised`
#ASSERT `a ground for refusal other than section 3 no. 4 applies` `grounds with only section 3 no. 8 raised`
#ASSERT `a ground for refusal other than a statutory duty applies` `grounds with only section 3 no. 8 raised`
#ASSERT `a ground for refusal other than section 3 no. 4 applies` `grounds with only section 4(1) raised`
#ASSERT `a ground for refusal other than a statutory duty applies` `grounds with only section 4(1) raised`
#ASSERT `a ground for refusal other than section 3 no. 4 applies` `grounds with only section 5 raised`
#ASSERT `a ground for refusal other than a statutory duty applies` `grounds with only section 5 raised`
#ASSERT `a ground for refusal other than section 3 no. 4 applies` `grounds with only section 6 raised`
#ASSERT `a ground for refusal other than a statutory duty applies` `grounds with only section 6 raised`
-- § 3 no. 4 is not 'a ground other than § 3 no. 4': the first composition leaves it out, as its name says; the second counts its limbs other than a statutory provision.
#ASSERT NOT (`a ground for refusal other than section 3 no. 4 applies` `grounds with only section 3 no. 4, other than a statutory duty raised`)
#ASSERT `a ground for refusal other than a statutory duty applies` `grounds with only section 3 no. 4, other than a statutory duty raised`

-- The list of grounds that apply. The request is: federal, prepared outside, submitted to the Council, not a recommendation, no other ground (a field the seat sets from the grounds), no other duty.
-- columns of `Request for a document`: 1 federal request; 2 prepared outside; 3 submitted to the Council; 4 recommendation or report; 5 another ground applies; 6 another duty attaches
--                                                           1     2     3     4     5     6
`the journalist's request` MEANS `Request for a document` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a request for the Council's own report` MEANS `Request for a document` OF TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE
-- With § 9(5) as in force the journalist's statement is confidential, a statutory duty under § 3 no. 4: that is the one ground.
#ASSERT elem `section 3 no. 4 by a statute` (`the grounds for refusing access that apply` `as in force from 1 August 2026` `the journalist's request` `grounds with nothing raised`)
#ASSERT count (`the grounds for refusing access that apply` `as in force from 1 August 2026` `the journalist's request` `grounds with nothing raised`) EQUALS 1
-- If the 2026 amendment is void the earlier wording covers only papers made inside: no ground.
#ASSERT count (`the grounds for refusing access that apply` `as before the 2026 amendment` `the journalist's request` `grounds with nothing raised`) EQUALS 0
-- The Council's own report is published under § 9(5) sentence 1: no ground on either reading.
#ASSERT count (`the grounds for refusing access that apply` `as in force from 1 August 2026` `a request for the Council's own report` `grounds with nothing raised`) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT count (`the grounds for refusing access that apply` `as before the 2026 amendment` `a request for the Council's own report` `grounds with nothing raised`) EQUALS 0
-- Two grounds at once: § 3 no. 7 (received in confidence) beside § 9(5) as in force.
#ASSERT count (`the grounds for refusing access that apply` `as in force from 1 August 2026` `the journalist's request` `grounds with only section 3 no. 7 raised`) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT elem `section 3 no. 7` (`the grounds for refusing access that apply` `as in force from 1 August 2026` `the journalist's request` `grounds with only section 3 no. 7 raised`)
-- If the amendment is void, § 3 no. 7 is the only ground left.
#ASSERT count (`the grounds for refusing access that apply` `as before the 2026 amendment` `the journalist's request` `grounds with only section 3 no. 7 raised`) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT NOT (elem `section 3 no. 4 by a statute` (`the grounds for refusing access that apply` `as before the 2026 amendment` `the journalist's request` `grounds with only section 3 no. 7 raised`))
-- A ground of § 3 no. 4 other than a statute (a Verschlusssache) is listed under its own name, and § 3 no. 4 by a statute is not.
#ASSERT elem `section 3 no. 4 by classification or by a professional or official secret` (`the grounds for refusing access that apply` `as before the 2026 amendment` `the journalist's request` `grounds with only section 3 no. 4, other than a statutory duty raised`)
#ASSERT NOT (elem `section 3 no. 4 by a statute` (`the grounds for refusing access that apply` `as before the 2026 amendment` `the journalist's request` `grounds with only section 3 no. 4, other than a statutory duty raised`))

§ `Part 3: the seat, input by input and case by case`

-- Each wrapper calls one export of bkv-ifg-seat.l4 with every input named, true if its name is in the list and false otherwise. A test then reads as the list of inputs the person ticks.
-- A misspelt name in a list ticks nothing, so a test that expects a ground fails loudly rather than passing by accident.

GIVEN trues IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`seat entitlement in force` MEANS
    `am I entitled to access with the grounds for refusal spelled out and section 9(5) BKV as in force` WITH
        `federal request` IS elem "federal request" trues
        `prepared outside` IS elem "prepared outside" trues
        `submitted to the Council` IS elem "submitted to the Council" trues
        `recommendation or report` IS elem "recommendation or report" trues
        `another duty attaches` IS elem "another duty attaches" trues
        `harm to international relations` IS elem "harm to international relations" trues
        `harm to Bundeswehr security interests` IS elem "harm to Bundeswehr security interests" trues
        `harm to internal or external security` IS elem "harm to internal or external security" trues
        `harm to supervision by a financial, competition or regulatory authority` IS elem "harm to supervision by a financial, competition or regulatory authority" trues
        `harm to external financial control` IS elem "harm to external financial control" trues
        `harm to measures against unlawful foreign trade` IS elem "harm to measures against unlawful foreign trade" trues
        `harm to a pending court case` IS elem "harm to a pending court case" trues
        `harm to a fair trial` IS elem "harm to a fair trial" trues
        `harm to an investigation` IS elem "harm to an investigation" trues
        `danger to public safety` IS elem "danger to public safety" trues
        `impairs confidential international negotiations` IS elem "impairs confidential international negotiations" trues
        `impairs the deliberations of an authority` IS elem "impairs the deliberations of an authority" trues
        `classified as a Verschlusssache` IS elem "classified as a Verschlusssache" trues
        `professional secret` IS elem "professional secret" trues
        `special official secret` IS elem "special official secret" trues
        `comes from another public body` IS elem "comes from another public body" trues
        `drawn in only temporarily` IS elem "drawn in only temporarily" trues
        `not meant to join its own records` IS elem "not meant to join its own records" trues
        `harm to Federal fiscal interests in commerce` IS elem "harm to Federal fiscal interests in commerce" trues
        `harm to economic interests of the social insurance funds` IS elem "harm to economic interests of the social insurance funds" trues
        `received in confidence` IS elem "received in confidence" trues
        `third party still wants confidence` IS elem "third party still wants confidence" trues
